  "question": {
    "text": "If the sum of the first 20 terms of the series<br/>$\\frac{4.1}{4+3.1^2+1^4}+\\frac{4.2}{4+3.2^2+2^4}+\\frac{4.3}{4+3.3^2+3^4}+\\frac{4.4}{4+3.4^2+4^4}+\\ldots$<br/>is $\\frac{m}{n}$, where $m$ and $n$ are coprime, then $m+n$ is equal to :-",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "ozGbJ",
      "text": "$423$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
